      "title": "Roll wear pattern",
      "description": "Feed tends to concentrate at the centre of the rolls, so the teeth wear fastest there (purple) and the rolls become \"hollow\" — the gap opens in the middle and the product coarsens. Spreading the feed across the full width (feeder width, chute design) and rebuilding or re-profiling the teeth keeps the gap even.",
